  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1159 AM CST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nAnother shortwave will move into the area on Tuesday. This is the \nday where there is potential for some snow across the region.... \nmainly over the central/eastern OK panhandles extending into the \nnortheast TX Panhandle. Precipitation amounts at this time look \nlight and any snow that falls is expected to be 1/2\" or less. Desi \nsnow probs for 1/2\" or less are high across the OK and TX Panhandles \nbut anything more than that and the probabilities quickly diminish \nto less than 20%. So the bottom line is that confidence is \nincreasing in seeing light snow across the OK and northern TX \nPanhandles but a very low probability of seeing anything more than\n1/2\" of accumulation. Some areas to to the south and west might \nnot see much of anything. This is still over 96 hours away so \nthere will be refinements as we go through the weekend. Another \nsystem could affect the area on Thanksgiving but at this time \namounts are still light regarding any precipitation. One item we \ndo have high confidence in is the much colder temperatures to \nstart off Thanksgiving week and continue for most of the week. As \nmentioned above, high temperatures will stay in the 40s with \novernight lows into the upper 20s and lower 30s.",
